source: tests/help_snapshots.rs
expression: out
---
Encrypted local secrets store.

Secrets are stored in a single AES-256-GCM encrypted file (default:
~/.config/ubertool/vault.enc). Override with --vault-file or
UBERTOOL_VAULT_FILE.

Password resolution: session cache → OS keyring → UBERTOOL_VAULT_PASSWORD
env → interactive prompt.

Usage pattern: --secret "$(ubertool vault get my-key)"

Usage: ubertool vault [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  init    Create a new empty vault
  set     Create or update a secret
  get     Retrieve a secret value
  list    List secret names (values are never included)
  delete  Delete a secret (requires --yes in non-interactive contexts)
  export  Export the full decrypted vault as JSON
  import  Import secrets from a JSON file (from `vault export`)
  unlock  Authenticate and cache the password for a session
  lock    Delete the session cache (idempotent)
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json
          Output as JSON to stdout. Human messages still go to stderr

      --vault-file <PATH>
          Path to the vault file (overrides UBERTOOL_VAULT_FILE and default)

  -q, --quiet
          Bare values only (pipe-friendly)

  -v, --verbose
          Verbose progress to stderr

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
